From 77c0b90346dc60ce8e84f4f57ee06f89a82948d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:17:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 130/152] domainset: a level of the trie is its keys one after
 another and a bit a node

The keys of a level are kept together, the ones that ended left out, and
a bit marks where each node begins, instead of a start and an end for
every node: 0.25 bytes a key for the nodes of two levels instead of 16.
A list of a JSON array is counted before it is read, so the keys are
gathered into room made once; the keys are let go before sing reads the
trie.

A rule set of a million names (21 MB of JSON), x86, GOMAXPROCS=4: the
peak RSS of ReadSource +100-110 MB before, +92 MB now. What is left is
mostly the copy domain.ReadMatcher makes of the trie while ours is still
held: without it the peak is +35 MB (measured with the trie handed over
in place, not committed).
